1. Set up

On ubuntu (WSL)

- sudo apt install python3-venv
- pip3 install virtualenv

Mac:
pip3 install virtualenv

# Creating the new virtaual environment
python3 -m venv venv

# Activating the virtual envirionment
source venv/bin/activate

# List all pip packages
pip3 freeze

# Install the pip packages for django
pip3 install django
pip3 install django-cors-headers

# Saving the pip packages to a file
pip3 freeze > requirements.txt

# Deactivating the virtual environment
deactivate

# Remoing the virtual environment and installing the packages from the requirements.txt
rm -r venv

# To install all the packages again from the requirements.txt
pip3 install -r requirements.txt











# Setting up the project
django-admin startproject chatbot (This will create the folder called chatbot inside chabot which is your main project folder)
There are many files but we will divide them into two parts:
1. The files we don't modify
    - __init__.py (Tells python that this folder is a python package)
    - wsgi.py (Python uses wsgi server for web development. This file contains basic configuration for your wsgi web server.)
    - asgi.py (Asgi is later standard on Python for web servers. This file contains configurations for asgi server.)

2. The files we modify
    - urls.py (Contains project URL routes. Example: store/ shows html page store.html)
    -  settings.py (Your main settings file. Contains application and middleware applications and project settings.)

# manage.py
There is also one file inside the chatbot 'manage.py' which is used to manage the project. 
script:     python3 manage.py runserver